      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T20:19:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: The comment says x64, but the original code included __i386__. This change effectively drops AVX512 support for 32-bit x86. Is this intentional?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 361,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 361,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "05f347d2f2a63113613f9b1b6bdf0ff0f4f66a40",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3fdca04b_e9e49043",
        "filename": "include/libyuv/row.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 361,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115898
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T22:03:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes this was intentional for 2 reasons:\n\n1. when building for windows, zmm6-15 are reserved so this CL avoids those registers for avx512, but that requires more than 8 registers for a few functions.  rather than attempt to make linux efficient and windows do pushes, i opted to make windows also efficient for x86_64 and just disable 32 bit\n\n2. realistically people with avx512 hardware will not be running 32 bit os/apps.  there are also complexities with 32 bit avx512 on windows emulator where float rounding is different than 64 bit and linux.\nalthough some row functions use 6 or less zmm vectors, its simplier to fall back on ssse3/avx2 for 32 bit x86.",
      "parentUuid": "12a6f6f2_c0acd93e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 361,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 361,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "05f347d2f2a63113613f9b1b6bdf0ff0f4f66a40",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
